The demos provided in theses directories illustrate how to do 
things with the NSL tools and components. The source code for
the demos is always provided. Users are invited to use the
source code to gather ideas and see how they could do things
for their own applications.

The demos are organized in various directories depending on
which products were used to build them.

drawlib: 
	Applications in this directory use only the Draw
	library. They illustrate how to program Draw library
	applications with Draw library, Motif and X function 
	calls exclusively. 

drawmaker:
	This directory contains drawfiles and images that you
	can load into XDrawMaker and experiment with. All the 
	drawfiles have been created with XDrawMaker. Some of
	them are animated, others are static. There are README
	files in each of the directories: drawfiles and images.


drawmaker_and_xfm:
	This directory contains examples of how XFaceMaker can
	be used as a complement to XDrawMaker. Examples cover
	the generation of C code for draw files built with
	XDrawMaker, and the use of XFaceMaker to build the interface 
	for applications using the XnslDraw widget. In some examples,
	the drawing's animation is programmed within XDrawMaker, while
	in others it is programmed directly in C code, with direct
	calls to the Draw Library functions.

xfm:
	This directory contains examples of how to do things with 
	XFaceMaker on its own.

xfm_and_drawmaker:
	This directory contains examples of widgets built with XFaceMaker
	from drawings made with XDrawMaker.


xnsltree:
	This directory contains examples of applications using the XTree
	widget, with or without using XFaceMaker.

